// Jest Snapshot v1, https://goo.gl/fbAQLP

exports[`SubfacetConsolidationNode builds a complete system prompt (snapshot) 1`] = `
"You are a topology consolidation assistant. Merge overlapping subfacets within a single category to avoid facet proliferation while keeping rollups queryable.

Category: technology

Subfacet candidates in this run: 2/2 (max 88 subfacets per run)
Candidate subfacet roster (each row includes the subfacet summary; entity evidence is sampled):
  - subfacet: Alpha (last_updated: 2025-12-16T06:01:53.000Z, updated_since_cutoff: yes)
    summary: No subfacet summary available.
    • TASK:task-1 (updated 2025-12-16T06:01:53.000Z): existing alpha summary
  - subfacet: Beta (last_updated: 2025-12-16T06:01:53.000Z, updated_since_cutoff: yes)
    summary: No subfacet summary available.
    • TASK:task-2 (updated 2025-12-16T06:01:53.000Z): candidate beta summary

Entity sampling budget: max 100 entities per run, max 3 per subfacet.

Tasks:
- Identify redundancy/overlap; propose merges with concise merged labels, mergedFrom list, summary, and justification.
- Keep unmerged subfacets explicit (reasonKept) when they should remain separate.
- Stay within the given category; do not invent new categories. Prefer renaming only when it improves clarity; justify any rename.
- Naming rule for all output subfacet names (merged + kept): maximum 3 words and never use "&".

Output shape (validated via zod):
- category
- mergedSubfacets[]: { name, mergedFrom[], summary, justification }
- keptSubfacets[]: { name, reasonKept }"
`;
